{% extends "quarterly_deep_dive/llm_prompts/base_prompt.j2" %}

{% set output_format_description = "a brief, objective observation (2-3 sentences) focused solely on the primary trend or key finding from the 'CVSS Score Distribution by CVE Category' chart data. No interpretation or recommendations." %}

{% block task_instructions %}
The chart titled '{{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('CVSS Score Distribution by CVE Category') }}' (typically a box plot or violin plot) displays the distribution of CVSS scores for various CVE categories (e.g., Remote Code Execution, Elevation of Privilege).
Examine the provided data summary for this chart.
Identify and describe the most significant observation. For example:
- Which CVE category has the highest median CVSS score?
- Is there a category with a particularly wide or narrow range of CVSS scores?
- Are there any notable outliers in CVSS scores for specific categories?
Focus only on what the data directly indicates about the CVSS score distributions for different CVE categories.
{% endblock task_instructions %}

{% block data_context %}
Chart ID: {{ data_context_payload.chart_id | default('cvss_score_by_category_chart') }}
Chart Caption: {{ data_context_payload.chart_caption | default('Figure 9. CVSS Score Distribution by CVE Category.') }}

Data Summary:
{{ data_context_payload.chart_data_summary | default("Data not available.") }}
Note: If percentages do not sum to 100%, this may be due to some CVEs lacking an assigned value (i.e., missing or NaN values were excluded from the calculation).
{% endblock data_context %}
